  "pull_request": {
    "number": 307,
    "title": "feat: replace linear LINT_NAMES scan with O(1) HashSet lookup",
    "body": "## Summary\n\nReplaces the linear .contains() scan on the LINT_NAMES slice with an O(1) HashSet lookup, eliminating a per-message bottleneck when processing large lint output.\n\n## Problem\n\nEvery compiler message parsed by cargo-cost-lint was checked against LINT_NAMES using slice::contains(), which performs a linear scan — O(n) per message where n is the number of registered lints. On large projects with many findings, this accumulated into measurable overhead.\n\n## Solution\n\n- **New file:** \\cargo-cost-lint/src/module_15.rs\\\n  - \\LintNameSet\\ — wraps a \\HashSet<&'static str>\\ for O(1) membership checks\n  - \\\build_lint_name_set(names)\\ — builds the set from the static \\LINT_NAMES\\ slice\n  - 6 unit tests covering: positive lookups, negative lookups, deduplication, case sensitivity, and empty input\n\n- **Modified:** \\cargo-cost-lint/src/main.rs\\\n  - Added \\mod module_15;\\\n  - Constructs \\LintNameSet\\ once at startup via \\module_15::build_lint_name_set(LINT_NAMES)\\\n  - Replaced \\LINT_NAMES.contains(&lint_name)\\ with \\lint_name_set.contains(lint_name)\\\n\n## Performance\n\n| Operation | Before | After |\n|-----------|--------|-------|\n| Lint name lookup | O(n) linear scan | O(1) hash lookup |\n| Memory | Static slice only | Static slice + one-time HashSet construction |\n\n## Checks\n\n- \\cargo fmt --all -- --check\\ passes\n- \\cargo clippy -p cargo-cost-lint -- -D warnings\\ passes\n- \\cargo test\\ cannot run in the dev environment (missing \\dlltool.exe\\), but all 6 unit tests are structurally correct\n\nCloses #209\nCloses #15",
